<title>CANADA: Ivaco to invest C$13 mln in wire business.</title>
<headline>Ivaco to invest C$13 mln in wire business.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivaco Inc said on Tuesday that it plans to invest C$13 million to expand its Sivaco Wire Group.</p>
<p>The group comprises four wire mills, two in Canada and two in the United States. The largest expansion is planned for its Newnan, Georgia facility, where state-of-the-art acid cleaning and annealing equipment is scheduled for startup in late 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>That plant expansion is directed toward the production and processing of sophisticated cold heading wire, Ivaco said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
</text>
